<div class="callout"><span class="callout__title">Note</span><strong>Critical Insight for Indian Kitchens</strong><p>Indian cooking involves oil splatter, steam and heavy chopping. Choose matte over high-gloss shutters for the cooking zone — they show fewer fingerprints and hide minor scratches better. Reserve gloss finishes for the pantry section or island, where daily wear is lower.</div>
<h3>The Master Bedroom — Sanctuary, Not Showroom</h3>
<p>The primary mistake homeowners make in modern bedrooms is over-designing them. A modern bedroom should feel like the most calming space in the home — not a showroom. The bed is the anchor, the wardrobe is the functional hero, and everything else supports a sense of peace.</p>
<p>Headboard Wall</p>
<p>Wallpaper, veneer panel or textured paint</p>
<p>Wardrobe</p>
<p>Floor-to-ceiling sliding doors</p>
<p>Lighting</p>
<p>Cove + bedside pendants + reading spots</p>
<p>Palette</p>
<p>Warm neutrals, no more than 3 tones</p>
<p>A floor-to-ceiling wardrobe with soft-close sliding doors in a matte finish is non-negotiable in a modern bedroom. Integrate dressing space, loft storage and a full-length mirror into the wardrobe unit itself so the rest of the room remains clear. The headboard wall deserves one considered treatment — an upholstered panel, a veneer strip, or a textured wallpaper — not a gallery wall.</p>
<p>Bedside lamps or pendant lights replace the harsh overhead light for reading and ambience. A false ceiling with cove lighting controlled by a dimmer turns the master bedroom from a sleeping room into a genuine retreat.</p>
<h3>Bathrooms — The Most Underestimated Space</h3>
<p>Indian homeowners consistently underinvest in bathrooms relative to what they get in return. A well-designed modern bathroom is the single space in the home that makes a daily, personal impression on you — and it significantly impacts the resale value of the property.</p>
<p>Modern bathrooms in India are defined by large-format wall tiles (600x1200 or larger) in neutral stones or concrete finishes, a wall-mounted WC, a floating vanity in lacquer or veneer, and frameless shower glass. Recessed niches in the shower replace soap dishes and shampoo shelves. Warm lighting around the mirror replaces the cold overhead light that makes everyone look unwell.</p>
